From: Siddhartha Srivastava <siddhartha@delphai.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 13:02:25 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] One-step proofs for providers (BuildOneStep, uwcctl onestep),
 pool bond basis capped at the reference unit cost, devnet agent vectors
 (build step 7)

- jobstate.BuildOneStep and FileWeights: a provider's ONE_STEP from its stage rows, the previous
  stage's rows, the job's tokens and a weights store; tested against a lying challenger on the
  tiny Qwen3 for both stage kinds.
- Pool claims are bonded against min(last payout, InitPrice). On the devnet the first delivery
  collected a large accumulated budget, and bonding new claims against that payout priced every
  provider out (the category would freeze). The payout already deters cheating by itself.
- getcategory/getjobstate report bondbasis and initprice; TestAgentVectors checks the agent's
  Python helpers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
